// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-10-28 (Wednesday): Today's date as pattern
// ============================================================================
// Weekly rotation slot: the calendar date itself drives the pattern. Today
// (IST) is 2026-10-28 -- day 28, month 10 (October), year 2026.
//
// THE DERIVATION (this is the whole point of the day):
//   Recent Wednesdays each found a different relationship between day and
//   month: a digit sequence (08-26), clock rates (09-02), a hocket when
//   day==month (09-09), two coprime grid-lengths (09-16), per-token
//   Euclidean flutters (09-23), a GCD-reduced polyrhythm (09-30), day/month
//   fed into euclid(7,10) (10-07), binary bits compared (10-14), and the
//   quotient/remainder steps of the Euclidean algorithm itself (10-21). None
//   of those used what's actually special about TODAY's day-number: 28 is a
//   PERFECT NUMBER -- its proper divisors (1, 2, 4, 7, 14) sum to exactly
//   28, the number itself (1+2+4+7+14=28, the same property shared by 6,
//   496, 8128). Month (10)'s proper divisors are only 1, 2, 5, summing to
//   8 -- 10 is DEFICIENT, falling short of itself by 2. That contrast
//   (day exactly fills its own number; month falls short of its own number)
//   becomes the whole structure, a genuinely different kind of number-theory
//   device from any GCD/ratio/binary trick used on prior Wednesdays.
//
//   DAY's bar is built from five motifs whose LENGTHS are its own divisors
//   -- 1, 2, 4, 7, and 14 tokens -- concatenated so the bar's total length
//   is exactly 28 steps: the divisors literally add up to fill the whole
//   bar, audibly mirroring 1+2+4+7+14=28. Three phrases alternate: CALL
//   orders the five motifs ascending by size (1,2,4,7,14 -- a widening
//   accumulation, sparse to dense); RESPONSE is CALL's exact token-for-token
//   retrograde (the whole 28-step bar reversed, a real retrograde device --
//   reversing the concatenation also reverses the motif order to
//   14,7,4,2,1, so the accumulation runs backward too); VARIATION reorders
//   the same five motifs (7,1,14,2,4) -- same material, a genuine
//   motif-and-variation device, not a new melody.
//
//   MONTH's bar is also 28 steps long (synced to DAY's bar) but only 8 of
//   those steps are pitched -- the sum of 10's proper divisors (1+2+5=8) --
//   the rest rest, audibly "falling short" the way a deficient number falls
//   short of itself. The 8 pitched tokens are grouped the same way, by
//   10's own divisor sizes (1, 2, 5), with rests filling the remaining 20
//   steps. Three phrases mirror DAY's structure at smaller scale: A places
//   the groups early-to-late with growing gaps; B is A's exact retrograde
//   (reversed bar); C reorders the groups (5,1,2) -- the same
//   retrograde/variation pairing as DAY, independently applied.
//
//   Structural tones use this project's established day/month-mod-7
//   mapping: day 28 mod 7 = 0 -> tonic anchors DAY (28 is a clean multiple
//   of 7, landing exactly on tonic -- fitting for the "exact" perfect
//   number). Month 10 mod 7 = 3 -> scale degree 3 anchors MONTH, as in
//   every prior Wednesday using this mapping.
//
//   CYCLES = 30 = day-digit-sum (2+8=10) + month (10) + year-digit-sum
//   (2+0+2+6=10). setcpm(90) x 30 cycles / 60 = 20s.
//
// Scale: F minor -- fresh for this slot (recent Wednesdays used B minor,
// C minor, and G minor); the divisor math is the idea, not the mode.
//
// NO DRUM KIT, deliberately, not by default: the perfect/deficient divisor
// grouping (dense accumulating motifs on DAY, sparse gapped motifs on
// MONTH) IS this piece's audible rhythm, read straight off today's own
// date digits -- a metric kit underneath would just restate a pulse that's
// already there, the reflexive-percussion failure MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md flags.
//
// Instrumentation, a fresh pairing from last Wednesday (10-21 used
// square+sawtooth): DAY gets `pulse` -- a synth basic (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md
// §2.5), harmonically busy enough to carry the acid taste layer on the
// denser, "complete" voice. MONTH gets `triangle` -- pure/soft (§1),
// matching the sparser, "falling short" voice. DRONE stays `sine` --
// tanpura convention, tonic and fifth, no automation (§2.5, §3). Only DAY
// carries the acid taste layer (light distortion + filter sweep); the
// sweep period (2 cycles) is GCD(28,10) = 2, the one factor day and month
// actually share -- a different, smaller role for a GCD-style number than
// the full ratio/euclid devices prior Wednesdays built whole structures
// from, here just flavoring the one automated parameter.
//
// This is a DAILY quick clip, not a flagship set -- one continuous pattern,
// no alap/jor/jhala arc.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(90)
let CYCLES = 30 // day-digit-sum (10) + month (10) + year-digit-sum (10)

stack(
  // DAY -- tonic-anchored (28 mod 7 = 0). Five motifs sized by 28's own
  // divisors (1, 2, 4, 7, 14 -- summing to 28, a perfect number) make up
  // the full 28-step bar. CALL orders them ascending (sparse->dense);
  // RESPONSE is CALL's exact retrograde (whole bar reversed, motif order
  // also reverses to 14,7,4,2,1); VARIATION reorders the same five motifs
  // (7,1,14,2,4) -- motif-and-variation on the same material.
  n("<[0 0 4 4 7 10 7 7 4 0 -3 0 4 7 0 3 7 10 ~ 10 7 4 ~ 0 -3 0 4 7] [7 4 0 -3 0 ~ 4 7 10 ~ 10 7 3 0 7 4 0 -3 0 4 7 7 10 7 4 4 0 0] [7 4 0 -3 0 4 7 0 0 3 7 10 ~ 10 7 4 ~ 0 -3 0 4 7 0 4 4 7 10 7]>")
    .scale("F:minor")
    .sound("pulse")
    .attack(.006).decay(.11).sustain(0).release(.05)
    .distort(.15) // acid taste layer, kept light so the divisor-motif shape stays legible
    .lpf(sine.range(500, 2400).slow(2)) // sweep period = GCD(28,10) = 2
    .gain(.32)
    .pan(.68)
    .room(1.1),

  // MONTH -- degree-3-anchored (10 mod 7 = 3). Only 8 of the bar's 28 steps
  // are pitched -- the sum of 10's proper divisors (1+2+5=8), 10's own
  // deficiency made audible as rest. A groups early-to-late with growing
  // gaps; B is A's exact retrograde (reversed bar); C reorders the same
  // groups (5,1,2).
  n("<[~ ~ ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 6 3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 3 6 10 6 3 ~ ~ ~ ~] [~ ~ ~ ~ 3 6 10 6 3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 3 6 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ ~ ~] [~ ~ ~ ~ 3 6 10 6 3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ 6 3 ~ ~ ~ ~]>")
    .scale("F:minor")
    .sound("triangle")
    .attack(.04).decay(.3).sustain(.15).release(.9)
    .gain(.27)
    .pan(.32)
    .room(2.6),

  // DRONE -- tanpura convention, tonic/fifth, held for the full piece with
  // no automation (the one moving filter this week lives on DAY instead).
  note("[f2,c3]/30")
    .sound("sine")
    .attack(1.4).release(2)
    .gain(.22)
    .pan(.5)
    .room(3.2)
)
